module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaCompact
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.LocalizingReflector

/-!
# Step 1 of Tag 09LK for the localizing subcategory generated by representables

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R` whose objects and whose
morphism modules live in one universe `v`, and suppose the homotopy category
`K = K(Mod^dg(C))` carries a triangulated structure — the structure that axioms (B) and (C) of
[Stacks, Tag 09P6] produce from a `DGCategory.ConeSituation`, which is not built here. Then for
any family `G : ι → ` of objects of `C` indexed by a type of that universe, the localizing
subcategory `N` of `K` generated by the representable modules `h_{G i} = C(-, G i)` admits an
exact reflector onto its right orthogonal, with a unit whose cone lies in `N` and which is
universal among morphisms into local objects.

This file carries no mathematics of its own. Its only purpose is to check that
`DGCategory.RightModule.preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_coyoneda_yonedaObjK` is the
hypothesis of
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_localizingClosure` on the nose:
the bridge is applied to the family of representables with no adapter in between.

## Universes

The bridge wants coproducts and a generating family indexed by the morphism universe of the
ambient triangulated category. For `K(Mod^dg(C))` with `C.Obj : Type u` and
`C.Hom x y n : Type v` that universe is `max u v`, because a homogeneous morphism of modules is
a family indexed by the objects of `C`, while the representables are compact for coproducts
indexed by `Type v` only. The statement below therefore takes `C : DGCategory.{v, v} R`, which
is the condition `u ≤ v` — satisfied in particular by a differential graded algebra, where `C`
has a single object. Nothing else in the development needs it.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK`: step 1 of
  [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for the localizing subcategory generated by a family of representables.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DGCategory

universe v r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

namespace RightModule

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R)
  [HasZeroObject (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K] [HasShift (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K] [IsTriangulated (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K]

/-- **Step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for a family of representable right differential graded
modules.** Assume the homotopy category of right differential graded `C`-modules is
triangulated. For a family `G` of objects of `C` indexed by the universe of the morphism
modules, let `N` be the localizing subcategory generated by the representables
`h_{G i} = C(-, G i)`. Then there is an exact functor `L` of the homotopy category and a unit
`η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` such that every `L X` is local, `η` is universal among morphisms into a local
object, and the cone of `η` lies in `N`.

The compactness hypothesis the bridge leaves implicit is discharged by
`DGCategory.RightModule.preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_coyoneda_yonedaObjK`, applied with no
adapter. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK {ι : Type v} (G : ι → C.Obj) :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L),
      (∀ X, (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal (L.obj X)) ∧
      (∀ Y, (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal Y →
        ∀ X, Function.Bijective fun φ : L.obj X ⟶ Y => η.app X ≫ φ) ∧
      (∀ (X Z) (f : Z ⟶ X) (g : L.obj X ⟶ Z⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
        Triangle.mk f (η.app X) g ∈ distTriang _ →
          (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v} Z) := by
  have : ∀ (i : ι) (α : Type v), PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete α)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (yonedaObjK (G i)))) :=
    fun i _ => preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_coyoneda_yonedaObjK (G i)
  exact exists_isTriangulated_reflector_localizingClosure fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
